sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as iPad (uploader)
    participant API as API Gateway REST
    participant L as Lambda handler
    participant C as photoChunks table
    participant P as photos table (feed)
    participant WS as API Gateway WebSocket
    participant B as iPhone (viewer)

    Note over B,WS: App in foreground → live subscription
    B->>API: getFeedChannel()
    API->>L: invoke
    L-->>B: { channel, wsUrl, token, connectToken }
    B->>WS: connect wsUrl?token=connectToken
    B->>WS: {"action":"subscribe", channel, token}
    WS-->>B: subscribe_success
    B->>API: listRecentPhotos(limit, knownPhotoIds)  (catch-up sync)

    Note over A: Capture → resize ≤2048 px → JPEG ≤640 KiB<br/>saved to on-disk queue first (offline-safe)
    A->>A: Base64 → split into ≤380,000-byte chunks (≤3)
    loop each chunk (parallel, 3 retries)
        A->>API: putChunk(photoId, i, n, data, createdAt, deviceId)
        API->>L: invoke
        L->>C: put item
    end
    A->>API: putPhoto(photoId, n, createdAt, deviceId, thumbnail)
    API->>L: invoke
    L->>P: put feed entry (only after all chunks)
    L->>WS: publish {photoId, createdAt} to feed/all
    WS-->>B: {"type":"message", data:{photoId, createdAt}}
    Note over A: queue file deleted → status "synced"

    B->>API: listRecentPhotos(limit, knownPhotoIds)
    API->>L: invoke
    L->>P: query GSI feed-createdAt (desc)
    L-->>B: newest photos (thumbnails only for unknown ids)
    Note over B: Grid updates without pull-to-refresh

    opt User taps the photo (lazy full-size load)
        B->>API: getPhotoChunks(photoId)
        API->>L: invoke
        L->>C: query PK photoId
        L-->>B: chunks ordered by chunkIndex
        B->>B: join → Base64 decode → UIImage
    end

    loop every 5 min while connected
        B->>WS: {"action":"ping"}  (idle timeout 10 min, subscription TTL ~1 h)
    end
